.TH DWM 1 dwm\-VERSION
.SH NAME
dwm \- floating X window manager for the wm environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dwm
.RB [ \-v ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
This configuration uses one tag and floating windows by default.
Focus follows the pointer across normal windows and monitors, including empty
monitor backgrounds. Docks never receive keyboard focus. Pointer focus does not
raise or relocate existing windows; clicking still raises them.
Keyboard placement affects only the focused window; it does not rearrange
other windows into a tiled layout.
.P
The status bar is disabled. The wm session provides an external compact tray;
dwm does not implement a tray or start session services itself.
New floating windows are centered once in their assigned monitor's usable area,
including transient dialogs on their parent's monitor. Docks and fullscreen
windows keep their own placement. Oversized floating windows start at the usable
area's top-left corner. Existing windows are not recentered on resize.
Borders indicate focus. Applications may request activation through
_NET_ACTIVE_WINDOW; this permits external run-or-raise tools to focus windows.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v
Print version information to stderr and exit.
.SH KEYBOARD
Super is the Windows key (Mod4). Alt is Mod1.
.TP
.B Super\-Space
Open wm-launcher: applications and session actions through dmenu.
Power and logout actions require confirmation in the launcher.
.TP
.B Super\-Return
Open, raise or cycle Alacritty windows through jumpapp.
.TP
.B Super\-w
Open, raise or cycle Brave windows through jumpapp.
.TP
.B Super\-Shift\-w
Open, raise or cycle Chromium windows through jumpapp.
.TP
.B Super\-e
Open, raise or cycle Thunar windows through jumpapp.
A background Thunar process without normal windows does not prevent opening one.
.TP
.B Super\-Shift\-m
Open, raise or cycle Spotify windows through jumpapp.
.TP
.B Super\-Shift\-c
Show CopyQ.
.TP
.B Super\-Left, Super\-Right, Super\-Up, Super\-Down
Place the window in a screen half. Combine horizontal and vertical directions
for quarters. Repeating a direction releases that axis; the opposite direction
switches sides. Releasing both axes restores the floating geometry.
Fixed-size windows are not resized. Application size hints remain respected.
.TP
.B Super\-m
Toggle maximization within the monitor's window area. Restore the previous
placement or floating geometry on the next press.
.TP
.B Super\-f
Toggle fullscreen. Geometry before fullscreen is kept separately from
subsequent resize events.
.TP
.B Super\-ntilde
Restore floating placement if needed, then center the window.
.TP
.B Super\-Shift\-Left, Super\-Shift\-Right
Move to the previous or next monitor, retaining keyboard focus.
.TP
.B Alt\-Tab, Alt\-Shift\-Tab
Focus the next or previous window in client-list order.
.TP
.B Super\-q, Control\-q, Alt\-F4
Request WM_DELETE_WINDOW on the focused window. The application handles
confirmation and unsaved data. Clients without this protocol are not killed.
.TP
.B Super\-Home, AudioPlay
Toggle media playback through playerctl. AudioPause pauses; AudioStop stops.
The default playerctl player selection applies, not only Spotify.
.TP
.B Super\-Shift\-PageUp, AudioPrev
Previous track.
.TP
.B Super\-Shift\-PageDown, AudioNext
Next track.
.TP
.B Super\-PageUp, AudioRaiseVolume
Raise the default audio output volume by 5%, limited to 100%, through wpctl.
.TP
.B Super\-PageDown, AudioLowerVolume
Lower the default audio output volume by 5%. Adjusting volume does not unmute.
.TP
.B Super\-End, AudioMute
Toggle mute on the default audio output through wpctl.
.TP
.B MonBrightnessUp, MonBrightnessDown
Adjust the first backlight device by 5% through brightnessctl, with a minimum
hardware value of 1. Requires backlight permissions; no external monitor DDC
support is configured.
.TP
.B Print
Open the interactive Flameshot capture UI. No automatic save is requested.
.TP
.B Super\-l
Run wm-launcher --action Bloquear. The session's xss-lock/i3lock integration
must be running; the shortcut alone does not provide a screen locker.
.SH MOUSE
.TP
.B Button1
Focus the clicked window and replay the click to the application.
.TP
.B Super\-Button1
Move the window while dragging. Manual movement releases keyboard placement.
.TP
.B Super\-Button3
Resize the window while dragging. Manual resizing releases keyboard placement.
.SH LAUNCH ERRORS
Commands started by bindings run through wm-run. Missing executables and early
nonzero exits are shown through Dunst, with an xmessage fallback. Slow applications
are left running; failures after the startup interval are not monitored.
Jumpapp uses foreground launch mode so early startup errors remain observable.
.SH CUSTOMIZATION
Edit config.def.h before generating config.h, or edit an existing config.h,
and recompile. There is no hot reload. Use the coordinator's make test to build
and validate temporary copies without installing or starting the programs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dmenu (1),
.BR st (1)
.SH NOTES
This is an unactivated development configuration. Do not start it over an
existing window manager. The wm repository documents preparation and the
future activation procedure. Report customization issues to the wm project,
not to the suckless upstream mailing list.
